# core.autocrlf is true for this repo, which is right for the source but must
# never be allowed near a binary: a zip whose CRLFs got "fixed" on checkout is a
# corrupt zip, and it fails at the person who downloaded it rather than here.
# Git's own heuristic already treats these as binary; this states it so a future
# .gitattributes cannot accidentally reclassify them.
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
